## Development

{% if package_manager == 'uv' -%}
Install [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/) and
create a virtual environment:

```bash
uv venv
source .venv/bin/activate
```

Install the package and its development dependencies:

```bash
uv lock
uv sync --group dev{% if docs %} --group docs{% endif %}
```

{% elif package_manager == 'pixi' -%}
Install [Pixi](https://pixi.prefix.dev/) and set up the development environment:

```bash
pixi install
```

{% else -%}
Install [Mamba](https://mamba.readthedocs.io/) and create the named environment
once, then install this project and its development dependencies with pip:

```bash
mamba create --file environment.yaml
make install
```

The environment name is `{{ mamba_environment_name }}`. If it already exists,
inspect it before installing dependencies; choose a different name rather than
replacing an unrelated environment. `environment.yaml` specifies Python and
pip, while `pyproject.toml` defines Python dependencies. They are not locked,
so future installs can resolve different versions.

{% endif -%}
{% if package_manager != 'mamba' -%}
Commit `{{ package_manager }}.lock` with the project. Run the test suite and checks with:
{%- else -%}
Commit `environment.yaml` with the project. Run the test suite and checks with:
{%- endif %}

```bash
make test
make lint
make typecheck
make build
make check-dist
```
